# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/

# Agent caches and metadata
.serena/
.claude-profile

# Per-session scratch written by the Qwen CLI. The directory is named after a
# session id, so every session leaves a new one behind; the contents are
# leftover prompts, not configuration. The rest of .qwen/ stays tracked.
.qwen/tmp/

# Per-developer Claude Code state, not shared configuration:
#   settings.local.json  — which plugins this developer has enabled
#   *.local.md           — per-project plugin settings, the convention both
#                          claude-code/example and claude-code/rtk-mcp-cc
#                          document ("belongs in .gitignore") but nothing here
#                          previously enforced
#
# settings.local.json is also covered by a global ignore on at least one
# machine, which is exactly why it needs to be stated here too: a rule that
# lives in one developer's ~/.config/git/ignore protects nobody else.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.md

# Release / Dist
dist/
